From 7c92bf1f6db55e58ab59bd9554f5ad4c5572ad2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 10:50:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(security): close cross-tenant access holes in API

Fixes 9 multi-user isolation/access issues found in audit:

1. Remove unauthenticated public attachment route (index.ts) that served
   any file by predictable name; browser now loads attachments via the
   authenticated, ownership-checked route with a ?token= param. Add path
   containment to that route.
2. email-webhook: drop hardcoded 'pis-webhook-2026' fallback secret.
3. claude-notes: scope all reads/writes by user_id (+ attribute inserts).
4. projects/reorder: constrain UPDATE to the current user.
5. ai/search: filter tasks/meetings by user_id.
6. ingest/status/:id: scope inbox item by user_id.
7. OAuth /auth (google/yandex/todoist): drop ?uid= identity spoofing.
8. tags: scope list/create/delete/link by user_id.
9. task dependencies: verify depends_on_id ownership before linking.

Frontend: add lib/attachments.ts helper to attach the auth token to
attachment URLs at render time and strip it before saving document bodies.

Builds (esbuild + vite tsc) pass; pre-existing test env failures unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0186L6QbAV4ME8XeDeh4MLgd
